  "canonical_title": "Stalls: Critical engine inoperative.",
  "subject_group": "Stalls",
  "versions": [
    {
      "designator": "25-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Flight",
      "title_at_revision": "Stalls: Critical engine inoperative.",
      "text": "(a) It must be possible to safely recover from a stall with the critical engine inoperative--\n  (1) Without applying power to the inoperative engine;\n  (2) With flaps and landing gear retracted; and\n  (3) With the remaining engines at up to 75 percent of maximum continuous power, or up to the power at which the wings can be held level with the use of maximum control travel, whichever is less.\n(b) The operating engines may be throttled back during stall recovery from stalls with the critical engine inoperative.",
